> And this seems to be a FlashInfer tactic selection issue. Maybe we should fix this in FlashInfer instead? cc @leejnau

Yes we should properly fix it in FlashInfer if at all possible.  We should not work around FlashInfer bugs in SGLang unless absolutely required.

@nbommi19, could you try [FlashInfer \#6331](<https://github.com/flashinfer-ai/flashinfer/pull/6331>) on your workload, using a build containing it with `FLASHINFER_TRTLLM_GEN_MULTI_WAVE_KV_SPLIT=1` and this PR’s SM-count override disabled? It would be useful to see whether the existing upstream heuristic recovers the benefit you measured.

